DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260718T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260718T113000
SUMMARY:Biltmore Estate: Walk the Westover Green and Blue Trails
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nLocated at The Inn on Bil
 tmore Estate\, the Westover Green and Blue Trails provide access to some o
 f Biltmore's beautiful woodlands. We will loop the Green Trail in a clockw
 ise direction\, pick up the Blue Trail to walk its entire length\, and the
 n go back to get the rest of the Green Trail.\n\nI estimate this to be abo
 ut 4.5 miles. The Green Trail is wide. The Blue Trail is of moderate width
 . These are relatively easy trails. There is a little elevation change\, b
 ut nothing particularly strenuous.\n\nWhen you drive to the Inn\, you will
  turn onto its access road. Near the entrance to the Inn is the entrance t
 o the parking area. There are two rows of parking\, an upper row closer to
  the Inn\, and a lower row a little further from the Inn. We will gather o
 n the lower row at the far end (away from the Inn).\n\nIf you need a restr
 oom prior to the walk\, Antler Hill is very close and there are public res
 trooms there. No restroom facilities are available during the walk.\n\nDre
 ss appropriately for the weather. Tennis shoes are fine\, unless it has ra
 ined a lot recently\, in which case you will probably want light hiking bo
 ots. Most won't want walking sticks\, though I plan to take just one. As a
 lways\, bring plenty of water and a protein snack. Dogs on leash are welco
 me. Strollers designed for trail use would be ok.\n\nThere is a grounds ad
 mission fee. We walk at Biltmore several times each year\, so an annual gr
 ounds pass is highly recommended.\n\nMany regular Biltmore guests have nev
 er walked the Westover Trails. I think you will enjoy these.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314601837/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260502T232908Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260502T232908Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
